# outline_group

Manages a manually maintained Outline group by UUID. Outline assigns the computed `id` during creation; do not set it in configuration. Renames update the existing group in place. This resource does not manage group memberships.

Use an unrestricted admin-owned Outline API key. The resource targets Outline 1.10.1 only.

Groups linked through `externalId` or synchronized from an external identity provider cannot be managed or imported with this resource. There is no `external_id` argument. Use the [group data source](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/glitchedmob/outline/latest/docs/data-sources/group) with a UUID to read an externally synchronized group without managing it.

## Example usage

{{ tffile "examples/resources/outline_group/resource.tf" }}

`name` is required. Omitting `description` sets it to an empty string; omitting `disable_mentions` sets it to `false`. Removing either argument from configuration restores that default on the next apply.

Outline 1.10.1 does not store a description supplied during group creation. The provider sets the description with a follow-up update. If that update fails, it keeps the created group ID in state, but Terraform taints failed creates. Fix the API error, then run `terraform untaint outline_group.engineering` using your resource address before applying again. The next apply updates the existing group. Without untainting, Terraform plans to replace it, which can discard memberships added since creation.

Refresh removes missing groups from state. Outline 1.10.1 returns an authorization error for missing IDs, so the provider verifies the caller is an admin and checks every page of the unfiltered workspace group list before treating that error as absence. If the group is listed or either verification fails, refresh returns an error and retains state.

An unexpected `groups.delete` 404 does not prove deletion. The provider rechecks the group using `groups.info` and, when needed, admin verification and the complete workspace group list. A still-present group, failed verification, or malformed response returns an error and retains state.

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Import

Import uses the group's UUID, not its name or external identifier. Replace the example UUID with the existing group's ID.

{{ codefile "shell" .ImportFile }}

Configure the resource to match the existing group's name, description, and mention setting before applying. Import reads the current values into state, but omitted optional arguments still apply their defaults on the next plan.
